# L §6.1 (round 14): "The two sides are of one sort: two kinds declared alike (the same clauses, legs and attributes,
# and the same parent ...; their notes aside), two things of one base kind ..., two rows of one type, or two movements;
# any other pair is refused (LOAD-SAME)"; L §8.3 LOAD-SAME "same <p> = <q>: <what p is> and <what q is>". a.persons is a
# kind, b.ben a thing: LOAD-SAME. (Writer 6's U-15/U-20, was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §6.1.)
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "e438b0e9e801813f005290db20ae57dbafcfc06810324f3ba998080e5c2db6c3"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "62b0623690f8004e28037173884be55e87162cbbd244eb89cae891e9e3867ce4"
  same a.persons = b.ben
ask n: count(p in a.persons on 2026-06-01)
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place wsp: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input income[p in persons]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ana, ola] lives 2000-01-01..
  income[ana] = 100.00 PLN "umowa"
  income[ola] = 10.00 PLN "umowa"
  opening[wsp] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
place wsp: accounts PLN lives 2019-01-01..
input pocket[p in persons]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  persons + [ben, ola_k] lives 2000-01-01..
  pocket[ben] = 50.00 PLN "umowa"
  pocket[ola_k] = 5.00 PLN "umowa"
  opening[wsp] = 1 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-SAME same a.persons = b.ben: a kind and a thing ...
